DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(sqrt(x))^2-2*(x-5)+1");
$fun_1 = Formula("e^((cos(x)))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({-10, -9, -3, 0, 6, 7} - {-10, -9, -3, 0, 6, 7})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-10, -8, -3, -1} U {-10, -8, -3, -1}");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("[3, 14] U (-infinity, 19] U [3, 14] U (-infinity, 19] U ((-infinity, 19] U [3, 14]) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 19])");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((-infinity, 19] - [3, 14])");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(-infinity, 19] U (-infinity, 19] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [3, 14]) U (-infinity, 19]");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`0+9+13/4`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('12.25')}
---

[`12*14+18`] is equal to [_____]{Real(186.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \leq 19\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 3 \leq x \leq 14\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cup A \cup B \cup A \cup (A \cup B) \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`A \cup A \cap B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -9, -3, 0, 6, 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-10, -8, -3, -1\}`]
- [`C = \{-2, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`A - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 1, -7, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, 8, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<1, -7, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, 8, -4>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -7, 0>") x Compute("<6, 8, -4>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<1, -7, 0>") . Compute("<6, 8, -4>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -10, -10, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -8, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 9, 3, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -8, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, -10, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, 3, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-10, -10, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 3, 0>") x Compute("<-10, -10, 7>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -8, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>3)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
